{"pocket":{"id":"ea51f576-9090-4694-afd1-793a5a4b92eb","word":"pocket","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"of a size suitable for putting into a pocket","tags":["feminine","masculine"],"word":"de bolso"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"a pocket dictionary","bold_text_offsets":[[2,8]],"type":"example","id":"16a3dc28-ff28-488c-9c4d-49c4aa6dc08c"}],"links":[["size","size"],["suitable","suitable"],["pocket","#Noun"]],"glosses":["Of a size suitable for putting into a pocket."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"c167882a-d288-4c5b-9e9f-e75bf0e5e5d8"},{"examples":[{"tags":["collocation"],"text":"pocket battleship","bold_text_offsets":[[0,6]],"type":"example","id":"dbe2daaa-eac5-4d3e-9ea2-d2fc6c2ab7fc"},{"tags":["collocation"],"text":"pocket beach","bold_text_offsets":[[0,6]],"type":"example","id":"ae422625-ac3f-4957-9615-992ea6b04316"},{"text":"She ate, drank, worked, danced, and made love in exactly the same way: con brio. She came into the apartment like a pocket hurricane.","ref":"1990, Stephen King, The Moving Finger:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[116,122]],"id":"8a6533c8-c967-43bb-916d-bb11ede10020"},{"text":"“There is never a shortage of pocket [Neville]^([sic]) Chamberlains willing to sacrifice other people’s land for their own peace of mind,” Sikorski said.","ref":"2024 January 19, Larry Elliott, John Collingridge, quoting Radosław Sikorski, “Casting their shadow: how Trump, Putin and AI dominated talk at Davos”, in The Guardian, →ISSN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[30,36]],"id":"99826ec6-f804-4ab1-bcdd-baf58fc0cb4e"}],"links":[["Smaller","smaller"],["compact","compact"]],"categories":["English terms with collocations","English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"glosses":["Smaller or more compact than usual."],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"88a3fd85-5c37-4f72-b5ff-889eff5b0694"},{"examples":[{"text":"a pocket pair of kings","bold_text_offsets":[[2,8]],"type":"example","id":"349d9e08-5d6d-4915-8aed-1e8b458be585"}],"categories":["English terms with usage examples","en:Poker"],"links":[["poker","poker"],["hole card","hole card"]],"raw_glosses":["(Texas hold'em poker) Belonging to the two initial hole cards."],"qualifier":"Texas hold'em poker","glosses":["Belonging to the two initial hole cards."],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"ee315b1a-a292-4cb9-9e09-2f551c2a4c25"}],"related":[{"word":"bag"},{"word":"pouch"},{"word":"purse"},{"word":"sack"}],"synonyms":[{"sense":"of a size suitable for a pocket","word":"pocket-size"},{"sense":"of a size suitable for a pocket","word":"pocket-sized"}]},"pocketknife":{"id":"026bb3f8-80e9-43bf-a6d3-af84de8e7fe4","word":"pocketknife","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"small knife whose blades or tools can fold in its handle","tags":["masculine"],"word":"canivete"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Jimmy had a pocketknife, and he wandered into the drawing-room with it one day, alone, and reduced ten thousand dollars' worth of furniture to an indeterminable value in rather less than three-quarters of an hour.","ref":"1878, Mark Twain, Tom Sawyer Abroad; About Magnanimous-Incident Literature:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[12,23]],"id":"2239bbe5-a0c4-45d9-89b5-bcb270b8a0c0"},{"text":"The Army, the Navy, the Maritime Commission, and Lend-Lease demanded more and more pocketknives — for demolition kits, medical kits, aviators’ kits, electricians’ kits; knives with tools, knives with marlin spikes. The pocketknife attained a new status — as indispensable equipment for all men in uniform.","ref":"1944, Alfred Lief, Camillus: The Story of an American Small Business:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[83,95],[219,230]],"id":"82eddff5-8c59-47ac-996f-6f640603b83b"}],"links":[["knife","knife"],["handily","handy"],["folding knife","folding knife"],["blade","blade"],["tool","tool"],["ret